# ==============================================================================
# UNZA CSC 4722 — Distributed Systems P2P Cluster Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# Define the network endpoint (host:port) for each node in the cluster.
# Format: node.<id>=<host>:<port>  OR  <id>=<host>:<port>
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCENARIO A: Multi-Laptop Setup (Across Different PCs on Same Wi-Fi / Hotspot)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Connect all laptops to the same Wi-Fi or phone Mobile Hotspot.
# 2. On each laptop, open PowerShell and run 'ipconfig' to find its IPv4 address.
# 3. Enter the respective IP addresses below:
#
# node.0=192.168.1.10:8000
# node.1=192.168.1.11:8000
# node.2=192.168.1.12:8000
#
# 4. Launch the respective node on each laptop:
#    Laptop A: java -cp out Node 0
#    Laptop B: java -cp out Node 1
#    Laptop C: java -cp out Node 2
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCENARIO B: Single-Laptop Simulation (Default Localhost Cluster)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
node.0=127.0.0.1:8000
node.1=127.0.0.1:8001
node.2=127.0.0.1:8002
